{"title":"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(similar_to_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (similar to Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be a positive real number greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Find the least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that:\n</p><p>There exists a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea52612e84325c34205602adc7561e52813ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in(1,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> for which there exists neither a triangle of side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> with positive area, nor a triangle of side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40ef7a5d44e2884c6fcba4721db9147f7165b055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0dbfa28bcb1b0f91a6cab22d10ac26c25818e33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with positive area.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038e1cc5326cc5ca82b38f15c22ff13d12407a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{3+\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{3+\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"504\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01cb5a95a7cf6f3ec67a8735efa29ce55407d9f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&gt;\\frac{1}{a}&gt;\\frac{1}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" />.  Using the triangle inequality, we find \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9059181d4c2754b73bf1c41a41965c53a1cc8447.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a+1 &gt; b \\implies a&gt;b-1\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc32c35ab9185374efdc82a7a5b45f683f7cefad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a}+\\frac{1}{b} &gt; 1\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />\nIn order for us the find the lowest possible value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, we try to create two degenerate triangles where the sum of the smallest two sides equals the largest side.\nThus we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3041f077b976ffc37055a870542c7d0f26d83c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=b-1\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/0974cd3d7f89d6bde4fb19e184bcde625bdc9697.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b}=1\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />\nSubstituting, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be6aac0001819cc8fd46b3f6c4abd9405b74c41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{b-1}+\\frac{1}{b}=\\frac{b+b-1}{b(b-1)}=1\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a91ccb76bef11a34069e903d584155406f248d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2b-1}{b(b-1)} = 1\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8a2355ef9f70d0133b08b9af3537dbb0e5c01f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2b-1=b^2-b\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" />\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> using the quadratic equation, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45924a7146c220f53694631b0bcce80d43c8439.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^2-3b+1=0 \\implies b = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\ \\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}}\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28similar_to_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(similar_to_Solution_1)\">Solution 2 (similar to Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (similar to Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can form degenerate triangles from the given information. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd78bcb8d40ee2dc69cf5e7ca921a4e80b7b3b3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/879dabb77649220d88489df64a427e39e297a711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> must satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/c/e9cddd3f997abe42540a37d2c17635830750f8d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 1 \\le b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" /> to be degenerate in the first scenario. \n</p><p><br />\nSimilarly, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abbca42795c96138f8075cf84f15f11ad4e33f4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n} + 1 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the only condition that is guaranteed to form a degenerate triangle from the second instance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d30e81935fe39100bb65e26b43ac831f1468a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"81\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSolving the second inequality for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> (for more-easily apparent inequality manipulation) yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301fc68252ed98210ba0447198401f8bb288adf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\ge \\frac{a}{a-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"33\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/0578c2a2ee94622d94a2ce0d622236951e525319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt; a+1 \\ge \\frac{a}{a-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"140\" height=\"33\" /> for almost all positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8726d98aced2f3140dd77a2d8614c2e7674700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> (see note at the end). \n</p><p><br />\nThus, it suffices to solve the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/498f41cbabffc497448b128a3da071676ea61246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+1 \\ge \\frac{a}{a-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"33\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> whose only positive solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/f/d4ff401a3a8a53f9d2068545bd2da508ebaf1bc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ge \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nSubstituting back into the first inequality yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/c/95cb8cddd851e63d6bc7a08379dc422d7f0cbe5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{b \\ge \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"103\" height=\"53\" /> and thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa04d7a9bcbf1fe3f2037cbc5e763c4b6d2661d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Note: this solution assumes that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/7/c276f196956f21bc85e8369d12eb51d23e6a2840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.618$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, the points at which the last inequality. \n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>~baldeagle123\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the triangle inequality we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/8/cf8c51ee207718cc1107fb58ceca3bd78c58880f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f0b149cd862955388c4c6cca520f222edf8c1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 1 \\ge b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9fbe6d121a333a5ae3dbaf997c4ad7bc69c0fca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+1 \\ge a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/26121063537cc3f563256cc3627e5e7cbbbcf6a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(1+a) \\ge a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/7/fe77dd74111ffdef9db2205f8d619699c8d47137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(1+b) \\ge b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a5d6513176c4b0545eb033ebb6e5219335e70ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b \\ge ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />. Clearly a triangle can't have negative area so, our triangle must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> area which means equality must be obtained for all the inequalities above. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1d44dcff1fddd55dfcec7d58fd967ecdf245ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/6/006cd5731ebd1f7c9d5642b693efb3ae1d594f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+b)^2 = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"21\" /> which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/9/8391b04eb144bf1ee20e7a0901e272ec21456ca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 - 3b + 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/5548d9ddfb9e7b855f8b285ed6b8d870168aab4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"58\" height=\"41\" />. So the answer is C.\n~coolmath_2018\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872f7d92616ee2d8d6a5cc6e8021d3fa82e0d82a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+a \\leq b, \\quad \\frac{1}{b} + \\frac{1}{a} \\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"182\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8ea2c7fe2a6a87ed5a31c1f68cae8b8822039b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies a \\leq b-1, \\quad \\frac{a+b}{ab} \\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"221\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/29731b7c08be5abfb3d30c58f4c3c27bfcb8cc2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies a+b \\leq ab \\implies b \\leq ab-a \\implies b \\leq(b-1)a \\implies a \\geq \\frac{b}{b-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"529\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/413f323cc9cccbabb35d5e52bc69eb34b6dc8ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\therefore \\frac{b}{b-1} \\leq a \\leq b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"159\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e39fb5d7e0827fd8ee5e799eadf6ff4bc2a69f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b}{b-1} \\leq b-1 \\implies b \\leq b^2-2b+1 \\implies b^2-3b+1 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"444\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/6/686f931c90447dfaa0aa3d9b024895f6472d713d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b= \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{9-4}}{2}= \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"209\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa2985ec9a40fa2d1d1f5ea2d11947b16d8e695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>select C\n</p><p>~ Ji Yang\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Rigorous)\">Solution 5 (Rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d511b1f3e84dd1092cde62fbab8357570dbae87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;a&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42fd0b162086b8a81648a1d5d87282c79aecf7d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{b}&lt;\\frac{1}{a}&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThree sides cannot form a triangle if and only if the sum of the lengths of the two shorter sides does not exceed the length of the longest side.\n</p><p>It is given that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf14e8c9505e294cddb4b228a9dd43b0c9f636c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+a\\leq{b}\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/261dc9daf571d6e8515cfed4eff77ef39b64c9cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{b}+\\frac{1}{a}\\leq{1}\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The second inequality is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/233fc8a49918357d31909855cbb66f42ff99a9b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\leq{ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/9/a49fda0502aeb661f34f1e302119b9ba4ed4429f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-ab\\leq{-b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9b254983d1330fe9d35ed707af9531bc78dcef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(1-b)\\leq{-b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b3254db66c26bc5cf8249c17a14481660404ac41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq\\frac{-b}{1-b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b4b97b1c35ed15d859889c4fd2c12d8e985ff2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is negative)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/feec535bc1adadc9e2f010e3af612e68b6e79289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq\\frac{b}{b-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/feec535bc1adadc9e2f010e3af612e68b6e79289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq\\frac{b}{b-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" /> into the first inequality, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81e755874377501b19b6e9ec05158cf23e0377d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq{1+a}\\geq{1+\\frac{b}{b-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"173\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/3452ec6b56df682cb6ddbf60419b802ed6a18358.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq{1+\\frac{b}{b-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"108\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2c4c76b0e44d3583604e875c9c76d37745178fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq{\\frac{b-1}{b-1}+\\frac{b}{b-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"142\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a003fedd8a6aadaf3425b01f014a55fa6d18bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq{\\frac{2b-1}{b-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"86\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6dce76974d361a11e4eca134962df64e7f85bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(b-1)\\geq{2b-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3dcf0896441c33c0dcf7e4616e114e9326bb6b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is positive)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5be008322da1d655d31f1404d6e1a36f15d4af4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2-b\\geq{2b-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/342963fbbd6b1acd320b6376ba456d8d715c1a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2-3b+1\\geq{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> has to be greater or equal to both of the solutions to this quadratic equation or less than or equal to both of them. We have either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa983300b4e9b9ad88f893d8d17fd763ee806f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq{\\frac{3+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e968bc5c5b1f63f5dbe7bac2a64424f490ed19f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\leq{\\frac{3-{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" />. The latter is impossible because it will make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa983300b4e9b9ad88f893d8d17fd763ee806f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq{\\frac{3+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" /> is a necessary condition. We have found a lower bound for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Now we need to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/3329afb8fe5762cada6695ef8d24277b851eb5f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b={\\frac{3+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" /> can satisfy the conditions.\n</p><p><br />\nA value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that is just adequate to make a triangle degenerate might be useful. We choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41fe8fea6b202adb2573c7a756027e4b96d6e5d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b-1={\\frac{1+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"159\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/946d79faaff737d09459fab797c550376c4da1bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\frac{1+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}=\\frac{3+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"43\" />, which means that there is not a triangle with positive area with these side lengths.\n</p><p>We also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/51829306177128897721995d84a2a989630b7d3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\div\\frac{3+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}+1\\div\\frac{1+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"206\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/742f5c9dc25195e5b61a2c32a181dd91bbb9723e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{2}{3+{\\sqrt{5}}}+\\frac{2}{1+{\\sqrt{5}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"162\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f8722091678da02a43eab61fd44fcc293b53dc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{2({\\sqrt{5}}-3)}{({\\sqrt{5}}+3)({\\sqrt{5}}-3)}+\\frac{2({\\sqrt{5}}-1)}{({\\sqrt{5}}+1)({\\sqrt{5}}-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"330\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16ef5e426ee0e30ba6ebbd8a501f3906fad37ed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{2({\\sqrt{5}}-3)}{-4}+\\frac{2({\\sqrt{5}}-1)}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"209\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/3/7c39bdec29ea2a7e1c37b8090b466e2d14e6b280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{3-\\sqrt{5}}{2}+\\frac{{\\sqrt{5}}-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"162\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/0640818a6197f2736b3259f8a356f0fb27556268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, which means that there is not a triangle with positive area with these side lengths.\n</p><p><br />\nWe have shown that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> has a lower bound of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f549ea821ec6bfcb1a4a22c869185dd70ea3cfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{3+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"43\" />, and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/3329afb8fe5762cada6695ef8d24277b851eb5f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b={\\frac{3+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" />, there exists a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies the conditions. This completes the proof.\n</p><p><br />\nThe smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f549ea821ec6bfcb1a4a22c869185dd70ea3cfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{3+{\\sqrt{5}}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~G2JFForever\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B\">2014 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017233916\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.058 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.090 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 610/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 19163/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   25.829      1 -total\n 79.27%   20.475      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 19.55%    5.049      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12430:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017233916 and revision id 283745. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}